## 662: PASS, six values and the full integer-translation proof

Author a displays {3.7}={7.7}={-8.3}=0.7. These are the three frozen
values in the correct requested order for x, x+4 and x-12.
Author b displays {-7.4}={-57.4}={5.6}=0.6. These are the three frozen
values in the correct requested order for x, x-50 and x+13.

Author c keeps x any real and n any integer. It uses the same proof already
frozen: m=[x], m<=x<m+1, then m+n<=x+n<m+n+1, hence
[x+n]=[x]+n, and finally {x+n}=x+n-([x]+n)=x-[x]={x}.
No positive-only restriction, truncation rule or arbitrary-real-shift
generalization has replaced the source quantifiers.

ungraded and parts=[] are appropriate for the complete exercise containing
a proof: all a/b values and the c proof remain visible in displayAnswer.
